// -*- mode:c++ -*-

// Xspm extension -- scratchpad DMA instructions.
// Uses custom-0 opcode space (OPCODE5 = 0x02, full opcode = 0x0B).
//
// Instruction encoding:
//   spm.dma rd, rs1, rs2   R-type  funct3=0x0   Initiate async DMA
//   spm.dma.w              I-type  funct3=0x1   Wait for DMA completion

// spm.dma: R-type, reads Rs1 (DRAM source), Rs2 (byte count),
// Rd is both input (SPM destination address) and output (echoed back).
// Starts an async DMA transfer via the SpmDmaEngine.
def format SpmDmaOp(code, *opt_flags) {{
    iop = InstObjParams(name, Name, 'SpmDma', code,
        ['IsNonSpeculative'])
    header_output = BasicDeclare.subst(iop)
    decoder_output = BasicConstructor.subst(iop)
    decode_block = BasicDecode.subst(iop)
    exec_output = BasicExecute.subst(iop)
}};

// spm.dma.w: implemented as a Load from the DMA STATUS register.
// The SpmDmaEngine delays the response until the DMA is complete,
// so the CPU naturally stalls on this instruction.
//
// IsNonSpeculative: only issue this load when it reaches the ROB head,
//   guaranteeing that the prior spm.dma has committed and the DMA has
//   actually started before we read the STATUS register.  All prior
//   instructions (compute between spm.dma and spm.dma.w) will have
//   committed by that point, enabling DMA/compute overlap for double
//   buffering without an expensive pipeline drain.
//
// Removed IsSerializeBefore / IsSerializeAfter:
//   In compiler-controlled SPM the compiler guarantees data-dependency
//   correctness.  IsNonSpeculative already ensures all prior instructions
//   (including the spm.dma that started the transfer) have committed
//   before this load executes.  Dropping the serialize flags avoids a
//   full pipeline drain on every DMA wait, which is critical for
//   effective DMA/compute overlap in double-buffered kernels.
def format SpmDmaWaitOp(memacc_code,
        ea_code={{EA = 0xF0000018ULL;}},
        offset_code={{;}},
        mem_flags=[], inst_flags=[]) {{
    inst_flags += ['IsNonSpeculative']
    (header_output, decoder_output, decode_block, exec_output) = \
        LoadStoreBase(name, Name, offset_code, ea_code, memacc_code,
        mem_flags, inst_flags, 'SpmDmaWait', exec_template_base='Load')
}};
